{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1210444-the-chahkol\u00e0k-lost-clan-bloodline-homebrew","id":1210444,"title":"The Chahkol\u00e0k: Lost Clan/Bloodline Homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-23T09:13:36-07:00","id":1210444,"title":"The Chahkol\u00e0k: Lost Clan/Bloodline Homebrew","content":"Hi there!<br /> <br /> So, I'm planning on running a campaign set in Philadelphia one day and I decided that I'd like to have some representation for the native americans who lived in that region prior to European colonization. After doing some research I discovered that the Lenni Lenape peoples controlled that territory prior to colonization and when doing some research into them, I discovered a creation story that involved Frog (who was master of all water) killing Snake and eating him in order to gain control over a spark of fire made by the Creator. The spark was taken away and used to bring life to the world and I figured that the murderous Frog, master of water and hungry for the spark of life would make a good basis for the kindred I wanted to design.<br /> <br /> Now I'm not super familiar with the mechanical side of 2E, so hopefully I can get some help on how I might make things better mechanically from you all.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks in advance to all of you who choose to take the time out of your days to read this.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1q6mZALKLFRmbJWPxV1zwb-vIpr4kK2_dpdV8VlvxpIA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 04-23-2018, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T03:45:18-07:00","id":1210884,"title":"","content":"Just scanning through it, here is what I've noticed immediately:<br /> <br /> Their discipline is somewhat underwhelming at the moment. Especially the first three dots are covered better by Protean. 2e has had a bit of a power bump, compared to 1e.<br /> <br /> On the whole the discipline is very similar to Protean, in fact most of it's powers are already (implicitely) covered by Protean. What you might want to do is give them Protean in-clan and note that (for example) for Haven of soil these guys are allowed to melt in with (very muddy) water. Similar for the fifth dot, mist is (technically) water.<br /> <br /> I just mean that you should try to make life easier for yourself. That way you can devote more time and attention to the whole aquakenisis schtick. Because that one isn't covered by Protean <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T04:55:06-07:00","id":1210900,"title":"","content":"Seconding Howalt on their unique Discipline.<br /> <br /> As a whole new Discipline, hydrokinesis but with blood sounds cool, with the current powers split across it and Devotions derived from it. Or even follow what Khaibit 2E did with Obtenebration, and make it a series of Devotions that derive from combining one basic Devotion and other Disciplines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T17:29:38-07:00","id":1211236,"title":"","content":"First: Thanks to both of you for responding and I really appreciate your advice.<br /> <br /> Yeah the unique discipline is definitely heavily based on protean. I considered just straight up giving them protean, but I figured that taking protean wholesale might take something away from it being the unique Gangrel discipline and despite having several similar features, the protean discipline wasn't quite what I was going for. You both are right though, the drowning is very close to protean in a number of ways.<br /> <br /> I tried to differentiate the similar powers somewhat by leaning into the 'water' angle, but it certainly shows its roots. I'll try and give Obtenbration a look because that does sound interesting and like something that could be helpful.<br /> <br /> I know the discipline is very rough at the moment, but hopefully with advice from those who are far more knowledgable then I when it comes to the mechanics of second edition, I can make it into something viable and desirable for when I put the bloodline into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T07:08:46-07:00","id":1211396,"title":"","content":"Good to see another Philly-based game out there. : ) If you end up doing a setting doc or write up for the game, I'd be curious to see your process.<br /> <br /> I'm personally not a fan of the Lost Clan concepts, but that's a personal preference. It makes a lot of sense for local, NA cultures to have their own monsters.<br /> <br /> Were I going to reskin the concept as a more traditional bloodline, though, as others have pointed out: you could probably go a long way as a Gangrel bloodline.<br /> <br /> Standard format (though we'll see if that holds with Spilled Blood) seems to be to add a base-10 discipline, and give a custom perk of Merits / Devotions. Members get a base one free at joining, and others available for XP purchase after. And then the additional drawback as well.<br /> <br /> You've got the flaw (very similar to the Mara bloodline from the Circle of the Crone book). Bonus discipline as Vigor makes sense.<br /> <br /> I'd probably put the base 'perk' as something like:<br /> <br /> <i>When utilizing Protean or Animalism Chahkol\u00e0k may control or adopt the traits of aquatic creatures, even if they wouldn't normally be allowed under the predatory/scavenging purview.</i><br /> <br /> Right away that gives you a lot of flexibility and I think really covers many of your custom powers already.<br /> <br /> Protean Two (Predatory Aspects):<ul><li>(<i>existing</i>) Aquatic - [covers Freedom of Motion]</li> <li>(<i>existing</i>) Extra Sense - [covers part of Water Eyes]</li> <li>(<i>existing</i>) Feral Senses - [covers part of Water Eyes]</li> <li>(<i>new</i>) Froggy Legs - bonus to jumping checks</li> <li>(<i>new</i>) Turtleback - minor armor bonus</li> </ul>etc. (Definitely check out how the Kindred Senses work for 2E)<br /> <br /> Next - break down anything that you don't think you can slot into Protean 2 with custom Bloodline Merits or Devotions.<br /> <br /> <b>Master of Currents</b> (Protean 1 devotion) 1 XP - You may meld with liquids when utilizing Protean 1 in addition to earth. An advanced level of this devotion also exists. It requires Protean 5 and costs an additional 1 XP. When using Protean 5, the Toad may dissolve into the form of brackish water instead of smoke. Compared to smoke, the Toad loses the ability to float through air and may only flow along the ground, however, they may fully travel through any bodies of liquid.<br /> <br /> Culture wise I also think it could be interesting if you pursued the patron/sacrifice angle a little deeper. Though that could more be written up into their actions with the Danse (they seem a natural recruit into the Circle, for example). But it could be interesting if there was some formalized mechanical effect like a proto-Oath. Sacrifice blood into the water, gain a beneficial condition like Inspired or Steadfast. Though - that could all be covered by just the Toad using Animalism on behalf of the offer-er and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","user":"Holy","date":". 04-25-2018, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:01:38-07:00","id":1212256,"title":"","content":"Hey this is a lot of really useful stuff! thanks for adding it and I'll definitely keep it in mind as I design the next draft. I'll give the idea of being a Gangrel Bloodline some consideration, although I'm still leaning towards leaving them as a lost clan sort of deal, although you definitely make some strong points by way of being a bloodline.<br /> <br /> Yeah, as time goes on I'll need to dig deeper and lay out the culture a bit more. The current version is very bare bones and is half meant to provide the historical background that I was drawing on to create them in the first place.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks so much for your help and I too am glad to meet another Philly gamer! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}